# graywolf pin side constraints for snake_chip
#
# The 28 pin frame has exactly seven pad slots per side - counted from
# pads_ETRI/MPW_PAD_28Pin_IO.mag, which places 7 PIC cells on each of T, B, L
# and R.  Cross referencing pads_ETRI/games.cel2 against
# pads_ETRI/MyChip_Game_Package.txt shows how those sides come out of the
# package:
#
#     side T (7 pads)  ->  package pins 22..28
#     side B (7 pads)  ->  package pins  9..13
#     sides L and R    ->  pins 1..8 (VDD) and 14..21 (GND)
#
# So a part in this frame gets at most twelve signal pins, and this chip uses
# exactly twelve.  T carries the seven a person touches, B the five that go to
# the panel.
#
# Pins are grouped by function rather than one group per pin: a padgroup is
# what keeps pads adjacent, so the five joystick lines come out as five
# consecutive package pins and can be taken to one connector, and likewise the
# I2C lines.  That is the whole point of writing this file - the board that
# uses the chip is easier to lay out, and the pinout is predictable.
#
# permute is deliberately omitted: with it, graywolf may reorder the pads
# inside a group, and the joystick is far easier to wire in UP/DOWN/LEFT/RIGHT
# order.  Confirm the order that actually came out in layout/snake_chip.pin
# after `make place`; grouping holds either way, only the order within a group
# depends on this.

# ---- side T, package pins 22..28 : clock, reset and the 5-way switch -------
padgroup Joystick
twpin_JS_UP                     nonfixed
twpin_JS_DOWN                   nonfixed
twpin_JS_LEFT                   nonfixed
twpin_JS_RIGHT                  nonfixed
twpin_JS_OK                     nonfixed
restrict side T

padgroup System
twpin_CLK                       nonfixed
twpin_RST_N                     nonfixed
restrict side T

# ---- side B, package pins 9..13 : the panel -------------------------------
#
# SCL_OE, SDA_OE and SDA_I are three core ports that become two PADINOUT cells
# at chip_top (DO tied low, OEN driven, DI read back), so they have to sit
# next to each other or the pad ring wiring gets long.
padgroup OLED_I2C
twpin_SCL_OE                    nonfixed
twpin_SDA_OE                    nonfixed
twpin_SDA_I                     nonfixed
twpin_OLED_RES_N                nonfixed
restrict side B

padgroup Status
twpin_LED                       nonfixed
restrict side B
